UnitVotingRewardsManager::ClaimIncentives
├── when the recipient is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the checkpoint limit is zero
│   └── it should revert with ZeroCheckpoints
├── when the caller is neither the voter nor the veNFT operator
│   └── it should revert with NotAuthorized
├── when the program id is zero
│   └── it should revert with InvalidProgramId
├── when the program does not exist
│   └── it should revert with InvalidProgramId
├── when a claim exceeds the remaining program balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientProgramBalance
├── when the caller is the veNFT operator
│   └── it should claim successfully
├── given the program has not started
│   └── it should transfer nothing
├── given the veNFT never voted
│   ├── it should preserve the initial global checkpoint
│   └── it should transfer nothing
├── given the latest checkpoint is current
│   ├── it should not close the open interval
│   ├── it should pay only the closed intervals
│   ├── it should reduce the remaining program balance by the claimed amount
│   └── it should not revert
├── given a stale open interval
│   ├── it should close the open interval
│   ├── it should pay through the closed interval
│   └── it should advance the global claim pointer to the tip
├── given a stale open interval beyond the checkpoint iteration limit
│   ├── it should revert with StaleCheckpointHistory
│   └── it should claim the complete required interval after history is advanced
├── given an ended program whose end is reachable but the current timestamp is not
│   ├── it should advance global history through the program end
│   ├── it should not query the gauge for pending fees
│   ├── it should preserve fee accounting
│   └── it should claim the complete program reward
├── given a stale open interval and a same timestamp checkpoint with pending fees
│   ├── it should report no earned fees for the arriving allocation
│   ├── it should notify fees before the no user global point
│   └── it should keep the credited fee snapshot on the overwritten point
├── given a stale open interval and a same timestamp checkpoint with pending fees when the arriving allocation claims fees
│   └── it should transfer no fees to the arriving allocation
├── given a single permanent voter
│   └── it should transfer the full streamed amount
├── given a large accepted program and single permanent voter
│   ├── it should compute the full entitlement without overflowing on intermediate products
│   └── it should claim the full entitlement without overflowing on intermediate products
├── given a large accepted misaligned program and single permanent voter
│   └── it should claim without overflowing on partial-interval products
├── given a large accepted program and single decaying voter
│   └── it should claim without overflowing on decaying accumulator cancellation
├── given many minimum slope decaying voters and the maximum accepted program
│   └── it should not distribute more than the streamed amount
├── given two equal permanent voters
│   └── it should pay each voter an equal half of the stream
├── given a decaying voter alongside a permanent voter
│   └── it should pay each voter their voting power share
├── given a week misaligned program and decaying voter
│   ├── it should pay the expected decaying share
│   └── it should not distribute more than the streamed amount
├── given varied week misaligned program inputs and decaying voter
│   └── it should not distribute more than the streamed amount
├── given a decaying lock that expires before the program ends
│   ├── it should report the earned amount before claiming
│   └── it should stop paying at the stake expiry
├── given a voter checkpoints at the interval right boundary
│   ├── it should report no earnings for the boundary voter
│   └── it should not pay that voter for the previous interval
├── given several programs funding the same veNFT
│   └── it should claim each program independently
├── given the claimed reward is the wrapped native and unwrapping is supported
│   ├── it should emit the ClaimIncentives event
│   ├── it should unwrap the wrapped native
│   └── it should send the native token to the recipient
├── given the claimed reward is the wrapped native and unwrapping is not supported
│   ├── it should transfer the wrapped native as an ERC20 token
│   └── it should not send native token to the recipient
├── given the claimed reward is an ERC20 token
│   ├── it should transfer the reward as an ERC20 token
│   ├── it should not send native token to the recipient
│   └── it should reduce the remaining program balance to zero
├── given same token programs funding the same veNFT
│   ├── it should isolate interleaved claims by program
│   └── it should track each program's remaining balance independently
├── given a bounded claim over multiple user checkpoints
│   ├── it should pay only the processed user checkpoints
│   ├── it should advance the claim pointers by the processed count
│   ├── it should let a later claim pay the remaining entitlement
│   └── it should update the remaining program balance after each claim
├── given a bounded claim with a stale open interval
│   ├── it should not close the open interval when the claim stops short of the latest checkpoint
│   ├── it should pay only the processed checkpoints
│   ├── it should close the open interval once a later claim reaches the latest checkpoint
│   └── it should pay the trailing period on that claim
├── given a bounded historical claim beyond the checkpoint iteration limit
│   ├── it should allow the bounded historical claim
│   └── it should pay only the processed checkpoint
├── given a bounded claim that skips a zero power checkpoint
│   ├── it should count the skipped checkpoint against the limit
│   └── it should let a later claim pay the remaining
├── given a repeated claim after the decaying stake expired
│   └── it should pay nothing on the second claim
├── given a voter that reset before claiming
│   ├── it should report only the earned share before claiming
│   ├── it should pay only the share earned while voting
│   └── it should not pay for the period after the reset
├── given a repeated claim with no new closed interval
│   ├── it should report no remaining earned rewards
│   └── it should transfer nothing on the second claim
├── given a program misaligned with week boundaries
│   ├── it should report the full streamed amount before claiming
│   └── it should pay the full streamed amount
├── given a program ending mid interval at the latest checkpoint
│   ├── it should report the full streamed amount before claiming
│   └── it should pay the full streamed amount without overpaying
├── given program boundaries misaligned with the user checkpoints
│   ├── it should report the full streamed amount before claiming
│   └── it should pay the full streamed amount
└── given multiple voters over the full program
    └── it should distribute the streamed amount without over-paying
